    "inspection": "DSDT PS2K MSFT0001/PNP0303 ports60/64; I2CB.TPAD UNIW0001/PNP0C50 confirmed as 093A:0255 touchpad. INOU exposes generic EC ECRR/ECRW, WMI WMBC OEMG mailbox. No identified per-key lighting method. Opaque firmware mailbox semantics are not fully decoded by static AML inspection."
  },
  "evidence": [
    "All enumerated USB devices authorized. No 048d:600b (OpenRevo ITE per-key) or 048d:ce00 (4-zone). All six HID nodes attributed to touchpad or Razer mouse.",
    "Bound mechrevo hwmon probe requires EC0766 bit2=1. TUXEDO uniwill_interfaces.h names this BIT_1_ZONE_RGB_KB; uniwill_leds.h classifies it as 1_ZONE_RGB. This records a successful probe condition, not a newly sampled full byte.",
    "OpenRevo b7d2b526e60cd04965eadab21e606bdb1e1aa56e builtin model JIAOLONG/JIAOLONG Series project26 keyboard_type=SingleZone_RGB. This is series-level corroboration, not exact board BOM proof.",
    "Existing tested product color interface uses only RGB0769/076a/076b and0767 apply bit; no per-key addressing.",
    "Normal PS/2 input path alone cannot determine lighting topology. Missing USB device alone cannot prove physical absence; combined EC capability and model classification give stronger evidence."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "https://github.com/faintonce/open-revo/blob/b7d2b526e60cd04965eadab21e606bdb1e1aa56e/src-tauri/resources/builtin_models.json",
